Cloud Hypervisor support for the Redox base drivers.

1. pcid: read virtio BARs without size probing. Cloud Hypervisor treats the
   0xFFFFFFFF probe write as a BAR relocation request and fails with "Failed
   moving device BAR". Virtio BARs are reported as 1 MiB (MSI-X table at
   0x8000, PBA at 0x48000) and ROM probing is skipped.
2. virtio-blkd: do not derive the read length from the used-ring length. QEMU
   counts the status byte there, Cloud Hypervisor does not.

Upstream already carries the rest of the former series (modern virtio-blk and
virtio-net device IDs, non-transitional initfs entries, used-ring index wrap).

